@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Troubleshoot & Debug Azure Deployments";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to identify and resolve common issues when deploying applications in Azure.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Common Deployment Issues -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2>Common Deployment Issues</h2>
        <p>When deploying applications to Azure, several challenges may arise. Understanding common issues can help troubleshoot effectively.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Configuration Errors:</strong> Incorrect settings in app configurations or connection strings.</li>
            <li><strong>Authentication Failures:</strong> Issues with Azure Active Directory, service principals, or managed identities.</li>
            <li><strong>Networking Issues:</strong> Problems with Virtual Networks, DNS resolution, or firewall restrictions.</li>
            <li><strong>Scaling and Performance:</strong> Inefficient resource allocation leading to performance bottlenecks.</li>
            <li><strong>Dependency Failures:</strong> External services like databases or APIs being unavailable.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="~/css/images/AzureDevOps/troubleshooting-guide.png" 
                 alt="Troubleshooting Guide" 
                 class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Steps to troubleshoot common deployment issues.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Debugging Tools -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Debugging Tools in Azure</h2>
        <p>Azure provides multiple tools to help diagnose and resolve issues:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Application Insights:</strong> Monitors app performance and detects anomalies.</li>
            <li><strong>Log Analytics:</strong> Collects and queries logs from different Azure services.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Monitor:</strong> Provides alerts and metrics for proactive monitoring.</li>
            <li><strong>Kudu Console:</strong> Offers an advanced diagnostic tool for App Services.</li>
            <li><strong>Remote Debugging:</strong> Enables debugging directly within Visual Studio.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="~/css/images/AzureDevOps/debugging-tools.png" 
                 alt="Debugging Tools" 
                 class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure offers multiple debugging and monitoring tools.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step-by-Step Debugging Guide -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Step-by-Step Debugging Guide</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to troubleshoot and debug your Azure-deployed applications:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Check Deployment Logs:</strong> Use Azure DevOps or App Service logs to identify errors.</li>
            <li><strong>Enable Diagnostic Logs:</strong> Capture detailed information on app behavior.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Application Insights:</strong> Analyze telemetry data to pinpoint issues.</li>
            <li><strong>Test with Kudu Console:</strong> Access Kudu to inspect files, restart services, or run commands.</li>
            <li><strong>Perform Remote Debugging:</strong> Attach Visual Studio debugger to running Azure applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor Resource Usage:</strong> Use Azure Monitor to detect resource constraints.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices for Troubleshooting -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Troubleshooting</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Automate Monitoring:</strong> Set up alerts and monitoring for early issue detection.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Infrastructure as Code:</strong> Ensure consistent deployments with ARM templates or Terraform.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement CI/CD:</strong> Automate deployments to reduce human errors.</li>
            <li><strong>Regularly Update Dependencies:</strong> Keep libraries and services updated to avoid vulnerabilities.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>Debugging and troubleshooting are essential skills for maintaining Azure deployments. By leveraging Azure tools and following best practices, you can efficiently resolve issues and ensure smooth application performance.</p>
    </div>
</div>

